{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ModelsOfQous.SkewPoissonIntegration","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ModelsOfQous.SkewPoissonIntegration","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Basic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.formal_group_dim_from_genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.formal_group_dim_from_genus","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L95-L100","doc":"For the QOU application, the formal group has dimension related\nto the genus: dim = 2g = 8 when g = 4 (Descartes condition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tensor_dimension","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tensor_dimension","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L85-L93","doc":"The Frobenius relation (strong multiplicativity) is an identity\nof natural transformations:\n(Id ⊗ m) ∘ (Δ ⊗ Id) = Δ ∘ m\n\nAt the level of ℤ-modules, this encodes that the comultiplication\nis an algebra map. We verify the dimensional identity:\nif V has dimension d, then V ⊗ V has dimension d². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.integration_requires_good_prime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.integration_requires_good_prime","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L70-L83","doc":"The p-adic completion preserves the deformation: the ℤ_p-algebra\nstructure on Dist(G) arises by p-adic completion of the\nGröbner-Shirshov deformation of Dist(H).\n\nFor a prime `p ≥ 7` (the smallest prime not dividing `30 = 2·3·5`),\nthe integration is compatible with the Descartes braid structure.\nNote `p = 5` does divide `30`, so the good-prime bound is `7 ≤ p`,\nnot `5 ≤ p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GrobnerShirshovBasis.finite_basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GrobnerShirshovBasis.finite_basis","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The basis is finite (always true for formal groups). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GrobnerShirshovBasis.numRelations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GrobnerShirshovBasis.numRelations","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Number of relations in the Gröbner-Shirshov basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GrobnerShirshovBasis.numGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GrobnerShirshovBasis.numGenerators","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Number of generators of the enveloping algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GrobnerShirshovBasis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GrobnerShirshovBasis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GrobnerShirshovBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GrobnerShirshovBasis","kind":"structure","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L55-L68","doc":"**Gröbner-Shirshov basis data**: the combinatorial structure used\nto compute the deformation of the distribution algebra.\n\nThe basis provides a canonical set of generators and relations for\nthe universal enveloping algebra U(Lie(H)) deformed by π_<.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] Chapter 6, §Skew-Poisson integration ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.strong_mult_ok","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.strong_mult_ok","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Strong multiplicativity holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.strong_multiplicativity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.strong_multiplicativity","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Strong multiplicativity of the comultiplication\n(Frobenius relation preserved under deformation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.reduction_ok","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.reduction_ok","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Reduction property holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.reduction_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.reduction_holds","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The deformation preserves the reduction mod p\n(encoded as a boolean flag; the isomorphism is categorical). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.dim_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.dim_pos","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Dimension is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.dim","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Dimension of the formal group (number of coordinates). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.p_prime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.p_prime","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L39-L39","doc":"p is prime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.p","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L37-L37","doc":"The prime p over which the base formal group is defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewPoissonIntegration","kind":"structure","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.lean#L23-L53","doc":"**Skew-Poisson integration data**: the algebraic structure encoding\nthe deformation of a commutative formal group H over 𝔽_p to a\n(generally non-commutative) formal group G over ℤ_p via a\nskewed-Poisson structure.\n\nThe three key properties are:\n1. Reduction: G ⊗_{ℤ_p} 𝔽_p ≅ H\n2. Deformation: Dist(G) deforms Dist(H) via Gröbner-Shirshov basis\n3. Strong multiplicativity: (Id ⊗ m) ∘ (Δ ⊗ Id) = Δ ∘ m\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:skew-poisson-integration}`\nRef: [hazewinkel1978] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-35190-6 ","signatureChunk":0}]}